.TH PEIPKG-COMPOSE 1
.SH NAME
peipkg-compose \- assemble an offline Peios package root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peipkg-compose lock
.I MANIFEST
.RB [ -o " " LOCK ]
.br
.B peipkg-compose build
.I MANIFEST
.BI --out " DIRECTORY"
.RB [ --locked ]
.RB [ --update ]
.RB [ --record-xattrs " " FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peipkg-compose
resolves a declarative package manifest and assembles a new filesystem root.
It does not mutate the package database of a running system.
.PP
.B lock
writes the exact package versions and hashes selected from the configured
repositories.
.B build
verifies and extracts that closure into a fresh output root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --locked
Require an existing lock and do not resolve package versions.
.TP
.B --update
Resolve again and replace the existing lock.
.TP
.BI --record-xattrs " FILE"
Write implied security attributes as deterministic JSON Lines instead of
setting them on the output tree.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peipkg (1),
.BR peipkg-repo (1)
